From 44a215bfa27efaeb39444fc5fdb7558932005d3f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ericman2001 <ericman2001@hotmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 11:44:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 20/20] gpio: cros-ec: Don't fail to probe on an EC without
 GPIOs

cros_ec_dev adds the GPIO cell to any EC that reports the GPIO feature,
and some, such as the HP Googlebook's fingerprint MCU, report it with no
GPIOs. Registering an empty gpio_chip then fails with -EINVAL and an
error in the log. Return -ENODEV instead, quietly.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpio/gpio-cros-ec.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpio/gpio-cros-ec.c b/drivers/gpio/gpio-cros-ec.c
index b48b684d8..4f2f79564 100644
--- a/drivers/gpio/gpio-cros-ec.c
+++ b/drivers/gpio/gpio-cros-ec.c
@@ -174,6 +174,10 @@ static int cros_ec_gpio_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		return ngpios;
 	}
 
+	/* Some ECs, such as fingerprint MCUs, have the feature but no GPIOs */
+	if (!ngpios)
+		return -ENODEV;
+
 	gc = devm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(*gc), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!gc)
 		return -ENOMEM;
-- 
